# Build context for the root Dockerfile.
#
# The image installs Potato from setup.py and mounts the project at runtime, so
# the context needs only the package, the packaging metadata and the entrypoint.
# Everything else is either development tooling, generated output, or a
# researcher's data — none of which belongs in a published image.
#
# Excluding these is not only about size. annotation_output/ holds real
# annotator records, *.sqlite holds the project database, and admin_api_key.txt
# is a live credential; a stray COPY would publish all three to ghcr.io.

# Version control and CI
.git
.github
.gitignore
.gitattributes

# Python build and cache artifacts
__pycache__
*.py[cod]
*.egg-info
build/
dist/
.eggs/
.pytest_cache
.mypy_cache
.ruff_cache
.tox
.coverage
htmlcov
venv
.venv
env

# Development dependency set — a superset of setup.py that pulls pytest,
# selenium and the docs toolchain. The image installs from setup.py instead.
requirements.txt
requirements-test.txt

# Downloaded model weights (382 MB) — gitignored, fetched by `potato
# download-models`, and not a Python package, so pip never installs them. They
# reach the image only if an operator mounts them or runs download-models in a
# derived build. Browser-side segmentation needs none of it: ONNX Runtime Web is
# vendored under potato/static, which does ship.
potato/models

# Example projects (554 MB, much of it media). The image serves whatever mounts
# at /app, so it needs no examples of its own.
examples

# Tests, docs and the website build
tests
docs
site
mkdocs.yml
internal
plans
node_modules

# Generated Space bundles and deployment scratch
spaces-build
deployment
.potato

# Runtime output and credentials — never publish these
annotation_output
annotation_output*
*.sqlite
*.sqlite-shm
*.sqlite-wal
admin_api_key.txt
*.log
potato/templates/generated

# Local-only material
demo
recordings
screenshots
.deciduous
.claude
CLAUDE.md

# Editor and OS noise
.DS_Store
.idea
.vscode
*.swp
